# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | In Progress          |

Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a required-property rejection before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L56), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid undeclared properties through to the executor unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L31)).
- When an enum fails, its rejection names the property and the allowed values ([validated by: rejects an enum value with the allowed values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L83)).
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
- Registering an invalid static schema fails before the tool is stored, so callers receive an error that identifies the tool they attempted to register ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static schema without rereading it during execution](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L126)).
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates a function definition against the schema resolved for each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L103)).

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
import Ajv, {type ErrorObject, type ValidateFunction} from 'ajv';
import type {ToolDefinition} from '../../types/ai.js';
import type {OutgoingMessage} from '../../types/messages.js';
import {log} from '../../shared/logger.js';

const AJV_OPTIONS = {strict: false, validateFormats: false} as never;

export interface ToolResponse {
  result: string;
  clientMessages?: OutgoingMessage[];
  suppressAssistantResponse?: boolean;
}

export interface ToolContext {
  userId: string | number;
  sessionId?: string;
  workspaceId?: string | number;
  authHeaders?: {
    cookie?: string;
    authorization?: string;
    host?: string;
  };
}

export type ToolExecutor = (input: Record<string, unknown>, context?: ToolContext) => Promise<string | ToolResponse>;

export function normalizeToolResponse(response: string | ToolResponse): ToolResponse {
  return typeof response === 'string' ? {result: response} : response;
}

export type ToolDefinitionSource = ToolDefinition | (() => ToolDefinition);

export interface RegisteredTool {
  definition: ToolDefinition;
  execute: ToolExecutor;
}

interface StoredTool {
  definitionSource: ToolDefinitionSource;
  execute: ToolExecutor;
  schemaValidator?: ValidateFunction;
}

export class ToolRegistry {
  private readonly tools = new Map<string, StoredTool>();
  private readonly schemaCompiler = new Ajv(AJV_OPTIONS);
  private readonly functionSchemaValidators = new WeakMap<Record<string, unknown>, ValidateFunction>();

  private resolveDefinition(source: ToolDefinitionSource): ToolDefinition {
    return typeof source === 'function' ? source() : source;
  }

  register(definition: ToolDefinitionSource, execute: ToolExecutor): void {
    const resolved = this.resolveDefinition(definition);
    let schemaValidator: ValidateFunction | undefined;
    if (typeof definition !== 'function') {
      try {
        schemaValidator = this.schemaCompiler.compile(resolved.inputSchema);
      } catch (error) {
        const detail = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);
        throw new Error(`Invalid input schema for tool ${resolved.name}: ${detail}`, {cause: error});
      }
    }
    this.tools.set(resolved.name, {definitionSource: definition, execute, schemaValidator});
  }

  get(name: string): RegisteredTool | undefined {
    const tool = this.tools.get(name);
    if (!tool) return undefined;
    return {definition: this.resolveDefinition(tool.definitionSource), execute: tool.execute};
  }

  getDefinitions(): ToolDefinition[] {
    return [...this.tools.values()].map(t => this.resolveDefinition(t.definitionSource));
  }

  getPromptInstructions(): string[] {
    return this.getDefinitions()
      .filter(t => t.promptInstructions)
      .map(t => `${t.name}: ${t.promptInstructions}`);
  }

  getExamplePrompts(): string[] {
    return this.getDefinitions().flatMap(t => t.examplePrompts ?? []);
  }

  has(name: string): boolean {
    return this.tools.has(name);
  }

  /** Validation contract: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md */
  async execute(name: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, context?: ToolContext): Promise<ToolResponse> {
    const tool = this.tools.get(name);
    if (!tool) {
      log.warn('tool', 'tool not found', {name});
      throw new Error(`Unknown tool: ${name}`);
    }
    const definition = this.resolveDefinition(tool.definitionSource);
    const schemaValidator = tool.schemaValidator ?? this.getFunctionSchemaValidator(definition.inputSchema);
    if (!schemaValidator(input)) {
      const error = schemaValidator.errors?.[0];
      const reason = this.formatValidationError(error);
      log.warn('tool', 'input validation failed', {name, reason});
      return {result: `Invalid tool input: ${reason}`};
    }
    log.info('tool', 'executing', {name, inputKeys: Object.keys(input)});
    const rawResult = await tool.execute(input, context);
    const response = normalizeToolResponse(rawResult);
    log.info('tool', 'execution complete', {
      name,
      rawType: typeof rawResult,
      clientMessageCount: response.clientMessages?.length ?? 0,
      clientMessageTypes: response.clientMessages?.map(m => m.type) ?? [],
      suppressAssistantResponse: response.suppressAssistantResponse ?? false,
    });
    return response;
  }

  private getFunctionSchemaValidator(inputSchema: Record<string, unknown>): ValidateFunction {
    const cached = this.functionSchemaValidators.get(inputSchema);
    if (cached) return cached;
    const validator = this.schemaCompiler.compile(inputSchema);
    this.functionSchemaValidators.set(inputSchema, validator);
    return validator;
  }

  private formatValidationError(error: ErrorObject | undefined): string {
    if (!error) return 'does not match the declared schema';
    const details = error as ErrorObject & {
      instancePath?: string;
      dataPath?: string;
      params: {missingProperty?: string; type?: string; allowedValues?: unknown[]};
    };
    const path = details.instancePath ?? this.normalizeLegacyDataPath(details.dataPath);
    if (details.keyword === 'required') return `${path}/${String(details.params.missingProperty)} is required`;
    if (details.keyword === 'type') return `${path || '/'} must be ${String(details.params.type)}`;
    if (details.keyword === 'enum') {
      const allowedValues = this.formatAllowedValues(details.params.allowedValues);
      return `${path || '/'} must be one of ${allowedValues}`;
    }
    return `${path || '/'} fails ${details.keyword}`;
  }

  private formatAllowedValues(allowedValues: unknown[] | undefined): string {
    return allowedValues?.map(String).join(', ') ?? 'the declared values';
  }

  private normalizeLegacyDataPath(dataPath: string | undefined): string {
    if (!dataPath) return '';
    return `/${dataPath.replace(/^\./, '').replaceAll('.', '/')}`;
  }
}
